  Running into trouble means you stopped running *away* from trouble.
The big problem most players have is an uncontrollable urge to fight.
In melee.  

  I just watched someone on NAO handle a summoning Archon on the Plane
of Fire.  The player just went around it.  No problem.  (I was
flabbergasted.)


  There are two rules about the Elemental Planes and the Astral Plane:

  1.  Don't fight unless you have to.
  2.  You never have to fight.

  Yes, that means thinking ahead.  Bunchteen charged wands of
teleportation are the main item to bring.  

  Why the emphasis on travel speed?  The longer you muck about the
better the chance of a minor trouble snowballing into complete disaster.
(One player on NAO ended up suiciding after getting mobbed 5 deep on the
Plane of Air.)  The best way to get out of trouble in NetHack is to
avoid getting into trouble in the first place.  On the Planes frequently
that's the *only* way to get out of trouble.

  If you want to muck about do like jistanidiot and use wizard mode.
Don't risk a game you've put hours and hours of play into.  One mistake
and all your accomplishments will gone.  (The game set up this "house of
cards" aspect, not me.  I'm just telling you about it.)

