  Didn't someone do the math and find a breakpoint between AC:-45 and
AC:-50?  That said, I've found AC:-45 or lower helpful.  It may just be
psychological, but it's still a real benefit.  (Note again that your
Silly ascension had AC:-45.)

  The OP has the spell of protection: +4 AC right there.   Before anyone
says the spell of protection is useless, how many players would wear a
+4 ring of protection without even thinking about it?  The spell doesn't
take a ring slot, has no hunger cost, and can be used when necessary.

  Trimming +4 armor with the spell of drain life and re-enchanting could
give 3 more.  Getting the small shield up to +5 would give another 3
more.   (Remember that worst case the shield can be taken off in one
turn, a spell cast, and the shield re-worn in another turn.  Don't do
this in dangerous close contact with the enemy.)

  Switching to Elven boots could add another 2 points of AC, since they
can be safely enchanted at +5.  The OP is a wizard: Spell of Haste Self
instead of speed boots gives the same "very fast" speed.  Expert jump
spell is 25% better than #jumping boots.

  That's 12 more AC right there, and with minimal spell casting
interference and no loss of ability.  (Elven shield would add another 3,
but hurt spell casting badly.)

  Go for a +7 elven leather helm and that's 2 more extra points of AC.
This may actually be a good idea for an Elven wizard.  Wizmode testing
seems indicated.   14 more points of AC:-51.  Even I feel comfortable
with AC below 50.  

  Stick with the Cloak of Magic Resistance.  At all costs!

  A lot of patience combined with a tame leprechaun and conflict could
allow jistanidiot to contribute gold over and over to the limit of -10
naked AC from purchased protection.


  Heck, jistanidiot could find/poly rings of protection and charge them
for even more protection.  (If they're edible things get *really*
interesting.)

  More divine protection can easily be gotten from another sacrifest
combined with luck manipulation.  There's no limit to the divine
protection available from this.  -92 AC has been achieved.  Really.

  All of those techniques require the ability to thrive on tedium and
annoyance.  (This is resented by some players.)  Lack of patience is the
big killer in this game.  Welcome to NetHack.


