  All that said, on Astral the combination of light source, jumping
(with boots), and bunchteen charged /oTele is practically unstoppable.
Spell of haste self and !oSpeed are great extras.   That's 3x traveling
speed.  

  Check my YAFAP.  I #jumped past Pestilence without being touched.
Twice.  Simply by not mucking about fighting until Astral was filled
with monsters.


  Posters will point out that zapping the Riders with teleport will
cause them to end up back next to you 11/12 times.  So what?  8/9 times
they won't be in your way any more.  (If they weren't in your way why
would you zap them in the first place?)


  Another great technique is area-effect weapons.  Area-effect means
multiple monsters are attacked at once.  b?oStinkingCloud, thrown lit
potions of oil, spells of FireBall and skilled+ Cone of Cold are
awesome.  These generally require a source of light:  Wand of light,
spell of light, scrolls of light, oil lamp, magic lamp, lantern,
candles, candelabrum of invocation (with candles), even wielded
Sunsword.

  They're tricky to use properly.  Read up on them and practice in
wizard mode to get good with them.

  /oLight as you pass through a room on Astral, then b?oStinkingCloud
into the crowd behind you while you check the Altar.  I did that once.
On the way back there were one or two monsters left that each took only
one stab to kill.  (No, I didn't need to kill them.  I was curious.)

  Skilled+ XL 30 Cone of Cold on the Plane of Fire does double damage to
fire resistant monsters.  A 3x3 area gets hit 2-9 times with 50+ damage
done per hit per square.  Oops, forgot to double it.  100+ points of
damage per hit per square.  9 squares hit per occurrence, done 2-9
times.

  The area affected 'wavers' around the targeted square with each new
hit.  That's actually good, because this is a spell with monstrous
overkill.  (XL 15 skilled+ Cone of Cold will kill Demogorgon twice over
with one cast, IIRC.)




